('980799625116780424', '🥜🍫 Peanut & Chocolate Bonbons – Creamy, Keto-Friendly & Freezer-Ready! By: @chiara.fiorani', '📊 Estimated Macros (per bonbon, est. – makes 5):\nCalories: ~60 | Fat: ~5 g | Protein: ~2.8 g | Net Carbs: ~1.5 g\n\nIngredients (Makes 5 bonbons):\n⅔ cup full-fat Greek yogurt (150 g)\n1 tbsp peanut butter (15 g)\n1 tbsp cocoa powder (8 g)\nKeto-friendly sweetener, to taste (I used sugar-free maple syrup, about 1–2 tsp / 5–10 ml)\nTopping:\nSugar-free dark chocolate, melted (about 1 oz / 30 g)\n\nInstructions:\nIn a bowl, combine the Greek yogurt, peanut butter, cocoa powder, and sweetener until smooth.\nSpoon or shape the mixture into bonbons and place them on a parchment-lined tray.\nFreeze for at least 4 hours, until fully firm.\nDip the frozen bonbons into the melted sugar-free dark chocolate.\nReturn to the freezer or fridge until the chocolate sets, then enjoy! 🫶🏼\n. #chocolatebonbons', '', '', '', 6062, 3299, 17, 0, 'Sat, 17 Jan 2026 12:28:51 +0000', '', '', '', ''),
('992058624200575056', 'Dreamy Raspberry White Chocolate Cake Roll Recipe for Joy', 'Elegant raspberry white chocolate cake roll recipe creates a heavenly dessert that impresses any guest. Grab a fork and experience pure bliss with every dreamy, fruity bite.', 'https://www.pictureperfectmeals.com/recipes/elegant-raspberry-white-chocolate-cake-roll-recipe/', '', '', 144, 87, 0, 0, 'Wed, 19 Nov 2025 12:02:12 +0000', '', '', '', ''),
('998321442472535097', 'Banana Cream Pie Recipe: Delicious Blended Chia Pudding Delight', 'Crispy edges, gooey center—this Banana Cream Pie Blended Chia Pudding will satisfy your dessert cravings without the guilt! Packed with the creamy goodness of bananas, chia seeds, and a hint of vanilla, this delightful recipe is a nutritious twist on a classic favorite. Perfect for breakfast or a sweet treat, it’s easy to make and loaded with healthy ingredients. Enjoy this delicious blend of flavors!', 'https://www.frostyrecipes.com/banana-cream-pie-blended-chia-pudding-recipe', '', '', 2804, 1150, 1, 0, 'Sun, 01 Mar 2026 22:10:35 +0000', '', '', '', ''),
